# Virtual environment
venv/

# Compiled bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# InferenceData (.nc): heavy binaries, regenerable by running the script that produces them
# (see PRODUCES in the header of each script). A fit of the linear model is ~90 MB and 2 minutes.
*.nc
*.nc.partial
*.nc.sha256

# Figures: every run of the battery rewrites them whole. They are artifacts, not sources.
model/*/plots/

# Tables that the results scripts rewrite on every run.
results/*.md
results/*.csv

# The LIVE dataset. The generator writes it in 5 seconds and it is deterministic by seed, so
# versioning it would mean having the same file twice in the repo: here and in
# synthetic_data/regimes/log__no_noise/, which is the backup against which config/log_regime.py
# fixes the scale of the priors. Two copies of the same file in two paths get out of sync; the
# backup is the one that rules, and step 1 of the README regenerates this one.
/synthetic_data/dataset.csv
/synthetic_data/media_share.csv
/synthetic_data/true_parameters.json
/synthetic_data/dataset_manifest.md
